<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Rounds the MediaView inside the native ad card. Applied to the FrameLayout
    wrapping it, together with android:clipToOutline="true" - MediaView is a
    FrameLayout subclass, not a ShapeableImageView, so it accepts no
    shapeAppearanceOverlay of its own.

    28dp is not arbitrary: nested rounded shapes look right when the inner
    radius is the outer radius minus the padding between them, and the card is
    40dp with 12dp of padding.

    This is required, not decorative. The media used to be square and got away
    with it because a 16dp card corner only reaches 0.51dp inward at 12dp down,
    leaving 11.5dp of clearance. At 40dp that same point is 11.43dp inward, so
    a square media block would clear the card's arc by 0.57dp - touching it in
    practice, and the same defect as the scrim that poked past the swipe card's
    rounded photo.

    Outline clipping is NOT antialiased, unlike a drawable's own corners. That
    was avoidable for the scrim, where matching <corners> on the shape did the
    job; there is no equivalent here short of wrapping in a MaterialCardView,
    which clips the same way internally. At this radius it should be fine, but
    it is the thing to look at on a real screen.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="@color/wedora_bg" />
    <corners android:radius="28dp" />
</shape>
